# Security model

Rocci's development server is loopback-only. That is a local-tooling boundary,
not an OS sandbox. The native host still has process authority.

| Boundary | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP host | `127.0.0.1` / `localhost` in `rocci.toml` |
| Browser origin | Same origin as the preview webview |
| Assets | Served from `/assets`; pin Datastar instead of loading a CDN by default |
| CSP | Default allows `'unsafe-eval'` for Datastar `Function` |
| Desktop bundle | Ad-hoc signed; not notarized |

`allowed_origins` is explicit. Do not widen host or CSP to “make Datastar work”
without naming the source you just trusted.

**Related:** [Status](/docs/status/).
